@zhuravel After some debugging, found that Rails 6.1 nows adds support for `scale` in  NumericalityValidator in commit: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/f72f743dc380d6b4f3518a8a1047414499b5a6c2

In the reproduction script provided above, since `scale: 2` is used on column `subtotal`. The value `999.999` is parsed and converted to `999.99` before validation check is ran in the validator. 

https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/71bc41477da96bb05edc33c1b6a42203e6999667/activemodel/lib/active_model/validations/numericality.rb#L76-L78
